#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124238 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "266a9a4e-cb11-5e4a-a2ac-c2e734966372" :question/math-academy-id "e-5424" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, and\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ 2x_{1} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -x_{1}\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n1. $A$ is not invertible\n2. $\\textrm{Col}(A)=\\mathbb{R}^4$\n3. $\\textrm{rank}(A)=4$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $4 \\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nCol(A) = R^{4}; dim(Col(A)) = 4 = rank(A); Null(A) = {0}; dim(Null(A)) = 0 = nullity(A)\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nwe conclude that\n$\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))=1 \\neq 0$.\nSo, according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ is not invertible.\n- Statement II is false. Since the matrix $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{Col}(A) \\neq \\mathbb{R}^4$.\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\textrm{rank}(A) \\neq 4$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124351 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "c1120305-c8cb-5f57-97b1-9b31dc059b4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9961" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n> *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{0}\\}$, then $\\text{__________}\\,$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n1. $\\det(A) = 0$\n2. $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$\n3. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n> $A$ is invertible $Col(A) = R^{n}; dim(Col(A)) = n = rank(A); Null(A) = {0}; dim(Null(A)) = 0 = nullity(A)$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{0}\\}$, then $\\det(A) = 0$.* $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$Since $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{0}\\}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ must be invertible, which means $\\det(A) \\ne 0$.\n- The following statement is true:$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{0}\\}$, then $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$Indeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{rank}(A)=n$.\n- The following statement is true:$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{0}\\}$, then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$ Indeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=n$, which means that $A$ has exactly $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124352 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "fff1daf8-5a1f-54c9-90d7-87710ca00d23" :question/math-academy-id "e-9962" :question/problem "$Col(A) = R^{n}; dim(Col(A)) = n = rank(A); Null(A) = {0}; W W W = 0 = nullity(A)$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. What should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the *invertible matrix theorem* states the following:\n\n> *Let $A$ be an $n \\!\\times\\! n$ matrix. Then we have the following equivalence:*\n> $Col(A) = R^{n}; dim(Col(A)) = n = rank(A); Null(A) = {0}; dim(Null (A)) = 0 = nullity(A)$\n\nThe missing expression is $\\textrm{dim(Null}(A))$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "879514d5-e127-5485-ab41-d459f6b5f379" :knowledge-point/title "Recognizing Parts of the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf819701-142e-5721-bf08-f1542a418f11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "nullity(A)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121274} {:answer/id #uuid "da6037e6-d4f8-5c11-bd91-79f38b4848a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121275} {:answer/id #uuid "0d3e06bb-7a81-55e1-9437-483e0a71b966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "dim(Col(A))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121276} {:answer/id #uuid "439b7207-a02a-5c87-9773-89e88bebcdda" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Null(A^{-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121277} {:answer/id #uuid "655e0036-f440-569b-9948-aae2a6a4fe9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "dim(Col(A^{-1}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d3e06bb-7a81-55e1-9437-483e0a71b966" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "dim(Col(A))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121276} :answer-field/id #uuid "e43bc06d-1111-5d7e-9966-e4dcf7ba21c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186121273}] :question/id #uuid "e871e5da-dd33-5fd3-8ed3-3fbed0583a91" :question/math-academy-id "q-141343" :question/problem "$Ais invertible⇔{Col(A) = R^{n}; W W = n = rank(A); Null(A) = {0}; dim(Null(A)) = 0 = nullity(A)$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n \\cdot n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125084 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb499f85-bc50-5330-84da-3dbf03f8f6e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123527} {:answer/id #uuid "11e014c7-fa9b-5761-8312-d3df2870f8ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} {:answer/id #uuid "1ecc6b01-a08a-5008-8ae2-e0b6bc1da0e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123529} {:answer/id #uuid "34c8d9c8-001c-5de2-94d2-056b747df4b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123530} {:answer/id #uuid "482d56f8-dca9-512f-8238-7a60e4045329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11e014c7-fa9b-5761-8312-d3df2870f8ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123528} :answer-field/id #uuid "42a1c7fd-d593-542d-877c-2e51b07b0213" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123526}] :question/id #uuid "7f4e1182-d195-5cca-bb1a-601ea1f9c921" :question/math-academy-id "q-47599" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n> *If $A$ is a $7 \\cdot 7$ matrix and $A$ is invertible, then $__________$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n1. $det(A) = 0$\n2. $Col(A) = R^{7}$\n3. $A$ has $5$ pivot columns"}]}
